{"id": "EUVD-2026-103912", "enisaUuid": "82e944dd-3c01-313c-8b35-4aaa86f8821f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: proximity: aw96103: validate firmware data length\n\nThe firmware parser reads a length from the binary header and then uses\nit to walk six-byte register/value entries. A truncated firmware image\ncan make the parser read beyond the copied firmware buffer. A value\nsmaller than the four-byte count field also underflows, producing a very\nlarge length.\n\nRead the little-endian field with get_unaligned_le32(), as previously\nproposed by David Lechner. Validate the header size, reject an\nunderflowed length, ensure the resulting payload is contained in the\nfirmware image, and require it to contain whole register/value entries.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a9b9f2d4e26589afd0ac099c8e5593170dd5ac7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6501b032be217ecf47e793b78a05078cf0b604ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/815ae0b73b69ace207b6bbf7ef428b06491c3ddb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a7c522a35477d70320bd64aba8e9de0c1058c6f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98658", "GHSA-h95c-5qhw-xc7v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10e5d679-e514-3029-9269-a76774a57621", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "2fddbc2a-8ca0-35d2-9683-f6f0a4e4bc39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3a543a20-3d38-3c10-b0a2-e207011433d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "4bf053ab-8848-3cdc-b019-a73f00db9d1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "96fc2d5e-349b-33c1-af46-0b0c4910904f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "989abf4d-b808-3a33-8d71-c26e50093a87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "aef0c2bf-c7cd-3160-92e1-418aa1da313e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07b241262dcad07671c444ca955903325de28e9e <4a9b9f2d4e26589afd0ac099c8e5593170dd5ac7"}, {"id": "b295803c-c4be-35ba-aed5-865bb38f3330", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07b241262dcad07671c444ca955903325de28e9e <6501b032be217ecf47e793b78a05078cf0b604ad"}, {"id": "b80b11d8-b39a-3ba1-991a-abcfda9820d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07b241262dcad07671c444ca955903325de28e9e <815ae0b73b69ace207b6bbf7ef428b06491c3ddb"}, {"id": "e1941c34-0a13-344e-98c3-32091dbbe381", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "07b241262dcad07671c444ca955903325de28e9e <1a7c522a35477d70320bd64aba8e9de0c1058c6f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8c42dabb-db79-3725-a43c-cc2f33ec9b42", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}